  "ingredients": [
    "8 ounce tilapia",
    "1 teaspoon chili powder",
    "1 teaspoon paprika",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)",
    "1/2 cup red cabbage",
    "1 tablespoon olive oil",
    "1 tablespoon lime juice",
    "1 teaspoon apple cider vinegar",
    "1/2 cup flaxseed meal",
    "1 tablespoon psyllium husk powder",
    "9 tablespoon water",
    "2 tablespoon olive oil",
    "4 tablespoon prepared guacamole"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Make half a batch of the Flaxseed Tortillas. Or you can always make a full batch and have leftovers to use in other recipes!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/tilapia-fish-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51073-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_3506.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chop up the red cabbage as thin as you can.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/tilapia-fish-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51073-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_24721.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dress the cabbage with olive oil, lime juice, and apple cider vinegar. Mix well and set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/tilapia-fish-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51073-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_2482.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Season tilapia with chili powder, paprika, salt and pepper to your liking. Do this for both sides.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/tilapia-fish-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51073-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_2487.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat olive oil in a pan and wait until it gets hot.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/tilapia-fish-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51073-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_2494.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add fish and cook on both sides for about 3 minutes each. You want the outside to be blackened.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/tilapia-fish-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51073-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_2501.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove the fish from the pan and set aside for a moment.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/tilapia-fish-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51073-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_2507.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Assemble tacos by placing fish, red cabbage, guacamole and sour cream (1 tbsp. per taco). Squeeze fresh lime juice over the top, then add a bit of cilantro.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/tilapia-fish-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51073-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
